From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: licheerv_nano: cap sdhci0 to 25 MHz for U-Boot

U-Boot's cv1800b_sdhci programs the PHY tap-delay only during UHS tuning,
which no-1-8-v disables. Its 50 MHz high-speed reads of the ~28 MB boot.sd
FIT are therefore marginal and fail intermittently ("Invalid FAT entry",
"Error reading cluster", "No partition table") even though the flashed
media is byte-correct. Cap sdhci0 to default-speed 25 MHz for reliable
reads. This is U-Boot's own DT copy, so the kernel's SD speed is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/dts/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts b/arch/riscv/dts/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
index 9871a75..e7b549f 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/dts/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/dts/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
@@ -38,6 +38,15 @@
 	no-1-8-v;
 	no-mmc;
 	no-sdio;
+	/*
+	 * Cap to default-speed (25 MHz). U-Boot's cv1800b_sdhci only programs the
+	 * PHY TX/RX tap-delay during UHS tuning, which no-1-8-v disables, so its
+	 * 50 MHz high-speed reads of the large boot.sd FIT are marginal and fail
+	 * intermittently ("Invalid FAT entry" / "Error reading cluster"). The FSBL
+	 * reads the same card fine at low speed; the kernel sets the delay itself,
+	 * so this only affects U-Boot.
+	 */
+	max-frequency = <25000000>;
 };
 
 &uart0 {
